From 25863f3668197cd45158d01b1e6208d32de367d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:28:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(2029): complete a failed back/forward scroll restore
 (downwards only)

Measured on PR1100: the browser restores the offset on back, but after forward the World
stayed at 0 instead of ~2750 because its content arrives later. scrollRestore2029 leaves the
browser in charge and only completes a restore it did not do: remembers each history entry's
offset (session storage, bounded; ignores the clamp caused by the page being swapped out), and on
POP waits (bounded) until the document is tall enough, then scrolls down to the offset if the
page is more than 40px above it. Never scrolls up, cancelled by touch/wheel/key/pointer, hash
navigation untouched.

